<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Union of Horodło</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1413</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Union of Horodło was a set of acts signed at Horodło on the Bug on 2 October 1413 by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o">Władysław II Jagiełło</a> and Grand Duke Vytautas. It renewed the union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> while keeping a separate Lithuanian grand duke. Forty-seven Catholic Lithuanian noble families were adopted into Polish heraldic clans, and Lithuania was reorganised into the voivodeships of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trakai">Trakai</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/union-of-horodlo.jpg" alt="Union of Horodło" width="320" height="315" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Poznaniak · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Grand_Duchy_of_Lithuania_(pink)_and_the_Crown_of_the_Kingdom_of_Poland_(red)_in_1386_-_1434.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
